tance and replay deadlines continue; returning does not create a new copy."}}}},
  ["unclaimed-dawn-court-2"] = {overview = {"Follow the named landmarks and the full text countdowns. Finish the current assignment before taking another.", "After an assignment resolves, allow at least 10 seconds of recovery. Scheduled routine pulses wait through assignments and recovery, then restart their full interval."}, roles = {{id = "tank", label = "Tanks", tips = {"Keep the alchemist clear of the reagent carrier's basin route."}}, {id = "healer", label = "Healers", tips = {"Follow the carrier and leave failed-reagent residue."}}, {id = "damage", label = "Damage dealers", tips = {"Prioritize the explicitly named catalyst guardian."}}, {id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"The carrier uses the basin named in that reagent announcement."}}}, phases = {{label = "Blood is not a signature", trigger = "Every 38 seconds", description = "A marked raider receives a 12-second reagent tether. Three stationary basins are named in text; the announcement specifies which basin neutralizes this reagent. The carrier stands within 10 paces for 3 continuous seconds. The same carrier is not selected twice in a row. A fresh cycle grants the alchemist a 30% incoming-damage ward, removed by correct neutralization; a failed cycle cannot stack another ward."}, {label = "Choose the antidote", trigger = "At 70% and 35% HP", description = "Two 16,000-HP vat guardians awaken, one protecting the raid's antidote and one the alchemist's catalyst. A basin names the catalyst guardian. Kill or control that guardian within 24 seconds."}}, abilities = {{name = "Blood is not a signature", summary = "Every 38 seconds", description = {"A marked raider receives a 12-second reagent tether. Three stationary basins are named in text; the announcement specifies which basin neutralizes this reagent. The carrier stands within 10 paces for 3 continuous seconds. The same carrier is not selected twice in a row. A fresh cycle grants the alchemist a 30% incoming-damage ward, removed by correct neutralization; a failed cycle cannot stack another ward.", "Success: The reagent is neutralized, removing the alchemist's next 30% damage ward.", "Failure: The carrier takes 900 poison damage; a 20-pace residue pool remains for 15 seconds, dealing 180 poison damage per 3 seconds to occupants. The pool never fills all safe floor."}, tags = {}, roles = {"tank", "healer", "damage", "everyone"}}, {name = "Choose the antidote", summary = "At 70% and 35% HP", description = {"Two 16,000-HP vat guardians awaken, one protecting the raid's antidote and one the alchemist's catalyst. A basin names the catalyst guardian. Kill or control that guardian within 24 seconds.", "Success: The catalyst is suppressed; the antidote gives the raid 450 HP over three ticks.", "Failure: The alchemist heals 3% maximum HP once. Both guardians become normally vulnerable after the check; there is no permanently wrong route."}, tags = {}, roles = {"tank", "healer", "damage", "everyone"}}}, sections = {{title = "Entry", paragraphs = {"The raid leader asks Keeper Avel for this expedition with twelve to thirty-six eligible level-60 characters. The guide explains the leader's current attunement requirements. Combat is tuned for twenty-four to thirty-six characters."}, bullets = {}}, {title = "Wipes and return", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A wipe resets the unfinished encounter after ten seconds without a living engaged member in its arena. Completed encounters remain defeated.", "Follow named landmarks and text countdowns. Check every character's floor and position; pets and dead characters do not count for player assignments.", "Return to the existing expedition through its guide or DZ Manager. Original instance and replay deadlines continue; returning does not create a new copy."}}}},
  ["ssratemple-vyzh-dra-cycle"] = {overview = {"Advance the temple's serpent cycle and survive Vyzh`dra's leading-target death touch."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare a tank replacement for each death touch and keep track of the current cycle state."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The controller tracks the designated trigger kills and schedules the appropriate glyphed or runed serpent according to saved progression.", "Vyzh`dra the Banished begins his death-touch timer within one to six seconds of engagement, then repeats it every two minutes.", "The death touch chooses the leading target, substitutes a pet's owner, and removes listed divine-aura protections.", "The Banished form despawns after 25 accumulated minutes out of combat; its death can unlock the Cursed form when the cycle is at the correct stage."}}}},
  ["unclaimed-dawn-court-1"] = {overview = {"Follow the named landmarks and the full text countdowns. Finish the current assignment before taking another.", "After an assignment resolves, allow at least 10 seconds of recovery. Scheduled routine pulses wait through assignments and recovery, then restart their full interval."}, roles = {{id = "tank", label = "Tanks", tips = {"Hold the Receiver clear of both forge stations."}}, {id = "healer", label = "Healers", tips = {"Prepare for two separated 500-point pulses if both channels fail."}}, {id = "damage", label = "Damage dealers", tips = {"Control advancing constructs before the 22-second delivery deadline."}}, {id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Two non-tank volunteers must hold different stations."}}}, phases = {{label = "Two living objections", trigger = "Every 36 seconds", description = "Two collection channels start at named forge stations. Each needs one volunteer within 12 paces for 4 continuous seconds within the 12-second window; volunteers cannot tank the boss and one volunteer cannot satisfy both stations simultaneously. Channels are placed on the same open floor."}, {label = "Return to sender", trigger = "At 65% and 30% HP", description = "Two 14,000-HP collection constructs advance toward the forge for 22 seconds. Root, mez or kill them. Each delivered construct gives the boss a 9,000-point rune."}}, abilities = {{name = "Two living objections", summary = "Every 36 seconds", description = {"Two collection channels start at named forge stations. Each needs one volunteer within 12 paces for 4 continuous seconds within the 12-second window; volunteers cannot tank the boss and one volunteer cannot satisfy both stations simultaneously. Channels are placed on the same open floor.", "Success: Both channels break and the Receiver loses his 30% ward for 15 seconds.", "Failure: Each unbroken channel deals 500 magic damage to the raid, staggered 4 seconds apart; maximum 1,000 over the cycle. No simultaneous spike."}, tags = {}, roles = {"tank", "healer", "damage", "everyone"}}, {name = "Return to sender", summary = "At 65% and 30% HP", description = {"Two 14,000-HP collection constructs advance toward the forge for 22 seconds. Root, mez or kill them. Each delivered construct gives the boss a 9,000-point rune.", "Success: Stopped constructs leave the boss exposed.", "Failure: Runes cap at 18,000 and are ordinary damage absorption, not extra permanent maximum HP."}, tags = {}, roles = {"tank", "healer", "damage", "everyone"}}}, sections = {{title = "Entry", paragraphs = {"The raid leader asks Keeper Avel for this expedition with twelve to thirty-six eligible level-60 characters. The guide explains the leader's current attunement requirements. Combat is tuned for twenty-four to thirty-six characters."}, bullets = {}}, {title = "Wipes and return", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A wipe resets the unfinished encounter after ten seconds without a living engaged member in its arena. Completed encounters remain defeated.", "Follow named landmarks and text countdowns. Check every character's floor and position; pets and dead characters do not count for player assignments.", "Return to the existing expedition through its guide or DZ Manager. Original instance and replay deadlines continue; returning does not create a new copy."}}}},
  ["steamfont-cargo-clockwork-ambush"] = {overview = {"Follow the Cargo Clockwork to the ambush on its delivery route."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Stay with the clockwork and prepare for the three-enemy ambush."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The delivery trigger starts the clockwork's path and establishes a two-hour event lock.", "At the ambush waypoint, Hector, Renaldo and Jerald appear around the stopped clockwork.", "The route later returns the clockwork to its start; its death signals cleanup to the three ambushers."}}}},
  ["steamfont-yama-tolk-and-the-inactive-clockwork"] = {overview = {"Help Yama recharge the inactive clockwork by casting precisely on his cues."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare the required spell before starting and wait for each charge prompt."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A qualifying wizard follows the battery dialogue and says ready to start the test.", "Four charge stages provide five-second response windows; the script accepts spell 5596 while the charge window is active.", "Missing a cue fails the trial and resets the setup.", "After the fourth charge, the final stage advances the wizard's quest."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-animated-statue-plans"] = {overview = {"Stop the goblin construction effort before the animated statues overwhelm the mission."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Watch the reinforcement runner when engaging the warlord."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"After 25 qualifying kills, the goblin warlord appears.", "Engaging the warlord sends a guard to retrieve reinforcements.", "The returning guard signals the workers and activates a stone statue."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-best-laid-plans"] = {overview = {"Recover the temple plans and confront the opposing faction's contact."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare for the contact and both assistants before completing the handoff."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Looting the plans causes the contact for the current faction route to appear.", "The handoff produces an opposing contact with two assistants.", "The opposing contact loses protection and becomes attackable."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-guardian-of-the-sands-shogurei"] = {overview = {"Disturbing the sacred sands brings servants and eventually Shogurei into the fight."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Control servants as the garden activates and keep the group together for the guardian."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Sand trigger regions can call Stillmoon servants to defend the garden.", "Task progression activates Shogurei for the confrontation.", "During combat he can cast Denial of Flight on his target."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-keepers-of-strength-and-wisdom"] = {overview = {"Complete the Keepers' scroll challenges to release the Strength and Wisdom trials."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare for all five Strength protectors before accepting that trial."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Give the Keeper of Strength the four required scrolls to reveal the Spirit Keeper.", "Tell the Spirit Keeper you are worthy to summon five ancient protectors.", "The Keeper of Wisdom accepts its separate four-scroll set and sends the party to Sung Li downstairs."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-scales-of-justice"] = {overview = {"Recover the koi master's stolen gift after a drake ambush."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Track the usurper's escape instead of assuming the encounter is finished at 75%."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The mission handoff spawns a drake usurper and two conspirators attacking the koi master.", "At 75% health, the usurper casts its escape effects, teleports to a random listed position and clears hate.", "Find the escaped usurper and return the recovered quest object to the koi master."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-sickness-of-the-spirit"] = {overview = {"Trace the temple sickness through Nethran, the stolen scroll and Wong Li's betrayal."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare for new enemies at each dialogue and handoff, especially the final return to Wong Li."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The forest keeper's handoff reveals Wong Li, whose dialogue creates the bathhouse trigger.", "Crossing that trigger brings Nethran and two goblin laborers.", "Return the clue to unlock the librarian, then question the librarian to spawn the scroll thief and three underlings.", "The final handoff makes Wong Li attackable."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-tea-for-thy-master"] = {overview = {"Protect the tea master while defeating the poison master and his recurring pet."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Intercept the pets promptly and protect the tea master while finishing the poison master."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The tea master's mission dialogue spawns the poison master, a pet and two assistants.", "The poison master begins a pet timer 25 seconds after spawn; later pets arrive every 97 seconds.", "Pets seek the tea master, whose death is tracked by the mission."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-tracking-the-kirin"] = {overview = {"Follow the ordered footprint trail until it reveals the Elusive Kirin."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Follow each newly revealed footprint instead of skipping directly to the final location."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Each footprint interaction advances the trail to its next scripted location.", "The trail must be followed in sequence.", "The final step reveals the Elusive Kirin near the temple."}}}},
  ["stillmoona-trial-of-perseverance"] = {overview = {"Keep the gong's defenders occupied and defeat twelve goblins to draw out their warlord."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Maintain aggression on the goblins and prevent any disengaged defender from ringing the gong."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Tell Osashi 'ready' to summon four goblins and begin the trial.", "Killed goblins are replaced until twelve kills have been credited without a bell failure.", "At twelve credited kills, the Stillmoon warlord appears.", "Engaging a goblin cancels its bell timers; a disengaged goblin starts a warning followed by the bell. A bell failure summons an Ancient Stillmoon Guardian."}}}},
  ["stonebrunt-mountain-dragon-transformation"] = {overview = {"A dire panda reveals a mountain dragon when wounded."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Expect a fresh target at the panda's position and prepare before crossing 80%."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 80% health the panda attempts to spawn the mountain dragon at its current position.", "If that dragon is already present, the transformation is deferred and the health trigger is rearmed.", "A successful transformation removes the panda."}}}},
  ["westkorlach-grokui-the-slumbering-basilisk"] = {overview = {"Prepare for Grokui to replenish his health repeatedly while gaining melee strength."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Save healing resources and defensive coverage for the later, stronger cycles."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 80%, 60%, 40%, 20% and 10% health, Grokui sets his current health to 430,000 and raises his minimum and maximum melee hits.", "The health resets make the fight longer than one health bar suggests.", "Leaving combat returns him to full health and restores the opening melee tuning."}}}},
  ["swampofnohope-swamp-dragon-transformation"] = {overview = {"A dire leech reveals a swamp dragon when wounded."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Be ready to acquire the dragon as soon as the leech transforms."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 80% health the leech attempts to spawn the swamp dragon at its current position.", "If that dragon is already present, the health trigger is rearmed instead.", "The leech disappears when the transformation succeeds."}}}},
  ["tacvi-pixtt-kretv-krakxt"] = {overview = {"Kretv Krakxt repeatedly sheds a husk and releases stronger brood waves."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Clear each brood fully and save raid recovery for the final area-rampage stage."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 90%, 70%, 50% and 30% health, the boss disappears into a husk and releases four, five, six and seven hatchlings respectively.", "Kill the full brood to restore the boss; additional roaming reflections complicate later stages.", "At 10%, three hatchlings appear while the boss remains active, switches to area rampage and begins a 12-second spell cycle.", "The room seals early in the encounter and punishes attempts to leave."}}}},
  ["tacvi-pixtt-riel-tavas"] = {overview = {"Control unstable constructs as Riel Tavas locks the room and increases her offensive pressure."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Use controlled crowd control on unstable constructs rather than killing them beside the raid."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The room seals at 90% health. At 50%, she gains flurry and an additional timed attack.", "Construct spawning resumes at 30%, becomes faster and larger at lower health, and is joined by a venom cycle below 25%.", "Unstable constructs explode when killed. A construct observed mezzed begins a 30-second despawn timer while Riel remains alive.", "The 10% stage further strengthens flurry; a wipe reset restores health and unlocks the room."}}}},
  ["tacvi-pixtt-xxeric-kex"] = {overview = {"Xxeric trades defense for aggression, summons ukun and heals into a final rage."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Reserve resources for the health recovery at 10% and keep ukun controlled through the middle stages."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 90%, the room seals and the cleaver timer begins; subsequent health bands shorten its interval.", "At 70% she changes from flurry to area rampage.", "At 50% she summons ukun and starts the rage timer. The hounds have limited scripted replacements when killed.", "At 10% she casts a reset effect and restores her health to 40% for the final rage."}}}},
  ["tacvi-tunat-muram-cuu-vauax"] = {overview = {"Defeat Tunat's doppelganger, then face a second body that borrows the powers of earlier Tacvi bosses."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Assign leaders to call each borrowed form and carry add-control plans from the preceding bosses into the finale."}}}, phases = {{label = "Doppelganger", trigger = "First body", description = "Handle the living phylacteries and the ukun that activate at 40%."}, {label = "Borrowed powers", trigger = "Second body, 90% to 30%", description = "Adapt to the previous bosses in health-band order."}, {label = "Tunat revealed", trigger = "Second body at 20%", description = "Finish the true form through haste, rage and overlapping spells."}}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The first body's room seals at 90%; its ukun activate at 40%. Killing it immediately reveals the second body.", "The second body changes at 90%, 80%, 70%, 60%, 50%, 40% and 30%, reproducing Xxeric, Kretv, Riel, Kvxe, Yihst, Mordl and Shaldn mechanics.", "These phases mix hatchlings, unstable constructs, timed power gains, charm pressure, split images and rage.", "At 20%, Tunat returns to his own form with haste, rage and additional spell timers."}}}},
  ["tacvi-zun-muram-kvxe-pirik"] = {overview = {"Balance four aspects during Kvxe's meditation to prevent permanent increases in his power."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Split damage across the four aspects and stop damage when each enters its correct band."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"From 90% through 30% health in ten-point steps, Kvxe enters a 70-second meditation.", "Bring each of the four balance NPCs into the current target health band. The messages announce when a scale tips in your favor or falls out of balance.", "An unbalanced aspect increases the boss's attack speed, armor, melee damage or attack rating.", "At 20% he accelerates again for the finish."}}}},
  ["tacvi-zun-muram-mordl-delt"] = {overview = {"Mordl Delt divides into images whose deaths determine his health when he reforms."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Assign each image to a tank and focus kills during the timed split windows."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 90%, 70% and 50%, the boss becomes inactive and splits into two, three and four images.", "Defeat the images to force his return, or survive until the three-minute split timer expires. Kills reduce the reformed boss's health.", "At 30%, two additional images appear while the main body stays active and hits harder."}}}},
  ["tacvi-zun-muram-shaldn-boc"] = {overview = {"Shaldn Boc alternates increasingly long rages with shorter periods of weakness."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Rotate defensive coverage during rages and recover during the weakened intervals."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The first rage begins after 35 seconds in combat.", "As health decreases, rage increases melee strength and attack speed and lasts from 20 up to 65 seconds.", "Each rage ends in a 35-second weakened interval before the next begins.", "At 90%, the room seals. Thirty seconds out of combat resets health, melee tuning and the room."}}}},
  ["tacvi-zun-muram-yihst-vor"] = {overview = {"Yihst Vor escalates his melee pressure and finishes with area rampage."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Maintain charm recovery and keep the raid healed before the final area-rampage phase."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"His melee tuning changes at 90%, 75% and 50% health.", "Allure runs on a 90-second combat timer and activates charm helpers.", "At 20%, single-target rampage and flurry are replaced by area rampage.", "The room seals at the initial health threshold and pulls escaping hate-list players back."}}}},
  ["taka-takish-hiz-adventures-shared-rules"] = {overview = {"Complete the selected Takish-Hiz adventure while managing its timer and scaled enemies."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Check the active mission status and prioritize the required objective."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The adventure selects its objective, level and difficulty from the request data.", "Assassination targets appear after the required kills; collection completion counts looted objective items.", "Optional named enemies and traps vary the route, while success before or after the main timer determines full or partial credit."}}}},
  ["takc-quintessence-of-sand-and-ritana"] = {overview = {"Break the guardians' protection and handle Ritana's transfer of power to the Quintessence of Sand."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Plan Ritana's kill timing deliberately and keep control as the Quintessence becomes mobile."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The linked guardians share aggression and split into additional enemies when defeated.", "Keeping Ritana alive until the Quintessence reaches 20% sets the bonus chest condition.", "At that threshold the Quintessence unroots and becomes protected, while Ritana heals and becomes vulnerable.", "Defeating the remaining linked guardians removes the Quintessence's protection so it can be finished."}}}},
  ["cazicthule-gimlik-cogboggle-escort"] = {overview = {"Protect Gimlik while he studies the temple and survives its ambushes."}, roles = {}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter strategy", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Tell Gimlik you are ready only when the group can stay with him.", "Collect the attackers at each of his research stops.", "Defeat the tracker near the end and complete Gimlik's requested follow-up before leaving."}}}},
  ["cazicthule-ring-of-fear"] = {overview = {"Interrupt the sacrifice, survive the temple waves and face the avatars of fear."}, roles = {}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter strategy", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Engaging the high priest draws his guards into combat.", "After the priest falls, the linked sequence escalates through waves and the Avatars of Dread, Fright and Terror.", "Keep resources for the Avatar of Fear when the final stage becomes attackable.", "Finish the final avatar within its thirty-minute window."}}}},
  ["cazicthule-sickly-mosquito"] = {overview = {"Weaken the sickly mosquito for the quest interaction and prepare for its final disease cast."}, roles = {}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter strategy", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"At 25% health a capture check begins every fifteen seconds.", "The ranger must have dealt damage and hold the required capture tool in the primary slot; keep the mosquito alive while waiting for the capture check.", "If the mosquito dies, it casts Epidermal Rot on a random hated target."}}}},
  ["hohonorb-lord-mithaniel-marr"] = {overview = {"Defeating Ralthazor opens the confrontation with Lord Mithaniel Marr."}, roles = {}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter guide", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Clear the preceding temple encounter with Ralthazor to activate Marr.", "Marr’s activation lasts two hours. When that window expires, he returns to his inactive state once no longer engaged.", "Defeat Marr and speak with the planar projection that appears for progression credit."}}}},
  ["illsalinb-the-council-of-nine"] = {overview = {"The Avatar of the Council grows weaker as its nine council members join the battle."}, roles = {}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter guide", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Each ten-percent health step from 90% through 10% activates another council member and sends it against a random target on the Avatar’s hate list.", "The Avatar’s melee damage falls at each activation, but the raid must handle the accumulating council members. Assign pickup tanks before the next health push.", "Avoid pushing several thresholds faster than the raid can establish control of the newly active enemies.", "Leaving combat fully heals the Avatar, restores its original damage and rebuilds the council population."}}}},
  ["templeveeshan-aaryonar"] = {overview = {"Engaging Aaryonar also brings the linked named guards into combat."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare tanks or control for the linked guards before the pull."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"If still alive, Kal`Vunar and Nir`Tan immediately add the puller to their hate lists.", "The quest script defines this linked pull but does not add a timed health-phase sequence."}}}},
  ["templeveeshan-lady-mirenilla"] = {overview = {"Engaging Lady Mirenilla also brings the linked named guards into combat."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare tanks or control for the linked guards before the pull."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"If still alive, Gra`Vloren and Wel`Wnas immediately add the puller to their hate lists.", "The quest script defines this linked pull but does not add a timed health-phase sequence."}}}},
  ["north-tov-broken-accord-mirenilla"] = {overview = {"A seasonal North ToV side raid tuned for 24–36 level-60 characters, with up to three characters per player.", "Break six court oaths, then challenge Vulak's final judgment. Clear calls, fixed camps and assigned jobs give each three-character team time to respond."}, roles = {{id = "tank", label = "Tanks", tips = {"Hold Mirenilla beside Mirror Main Camp, facing away from the raid. Keep the dragon and the main raid clear of Isolation Witness."}}, {id = "healer", label = "Healers and curers", tips = {"Cover arcane pulses and maintain a healer in, or within healing range of, the marked team's refuge. Successful isolation still deals 900 damage to each nearby character."}}, {id = "damage", label = "Damage dealers", tips = {"Keep attacking from the main camp until your team is marked. Send at most three characters to the refuge and return after impact."}}, {id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Assign jobs by three-character team where possible. Read the named target, camp and countdown; check every character rather than moving only your main.", "Start each deadline healthy. A 75%-maximum-HP failure leaves little room for existing damage or the dragon's next attack."}}}, phases = {{label = "Break the oath", trigger = "Challenge to victory", description = "Resolve the court's repeating assignment on its 45-second cadence while maintaining damage and healing. There is no health-based phase change."}}, abilities = {{name = "Fractured Reflection", summary = "The named non-tank has twelve seconds to reach the Isolation Witness. Move that character's three-character team together.", description = {"The named non-tank has twelve seconds to reach the Isolation Witness. Move that character's three-character team together.", "At impact, the marked character must be within the refuge's 15-unit radius, on its floor with clear line of sight. Only one to three living player characters may occupy the 25-unit-radius blast around the mark. A correct small group takes 900 damage each.", "Missing the refuge or crowding the blast deals 75% of maximum HP to the marked character and nearby living players. Keep the main raid with the boss, away from the refuge.", "Death, disconnecting or zoning does not cancel the assignment. The blast still resolves at the marked character's last position if the target is lost."}, tags = {}, roles = {"everyone"}}, {name = "Arcane pulse", summary = "Recurring raid damage between assignments.", description = {"A routine raid pulse is scheduled every 25 seconds. Assignment warnings, wards and recovery postpone it; missed pulses do not build into a burst."}, tags = {"raid damage"}, roles = {"healer", "everyone"}}}, sections = {{title = "Entry and raid preparation", paragraphs = {"This side raid requires active Season 1 characters of level 55 or higher, with both personal and server Velious access. Combat and equipment are designed around level 60."}, bullets = {"In the public Temple of Veeshan, the raid leader asks Echo of the First Brood for The Broken Accord with 12–36 eligible characters. Each member then says ready to enter to the Echo.", "Inside, the expedition leader says challenge to the selected Oath Witness. Fight the six courts in any order, one at a time; completing all six reveals Vulak. Challenge his Oath Witness when ready.", "The first challenge locks the raid's combat budget, with a 24-character minimum and a 36-character maximum. A 12-character request keeps the 24-character tuning floor and both six-character soak requirements. Later roster changes do not reduce that budget."}}, {title = "Positioning and warnings", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Main raid: Mirror Main Camp. Marked team: Isolation Witness, within its 15-unit radius. Keep the rest of the raid more than 25 units from the marked character at impact.", "Use the named stationary landmarks on their flat floor, with clear line of sight. A matching camp icon confirms that a character counts as inside. Circles are an extra cue; follow chat calls and countdowns even when terrain makes them hard to see."}}, {title = "Timing and damage pressure", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The first assignment begins 45 seconds after the challenge. Subsequent assignments follow a 45-second cadence when the fight is ready.", "After an assignment resolves, there is an eight-second recovery before another scripted assignment or routine pulse. Boss melee generally continues. A failure dealing 75% to the current tank briefly pauses boss melee for two seconds.", "Percentage failures remove the stated share of maximum HP and bypass mitigation and absorption. They can kill an injured character; no one-HP survival floor applies. Recover before the next call.", "Soft enrage begins at eight minutes, adding 10% melee and another 10% every 30 seconds. Combined scripted melee increases cap at 50%."}}, {title = "Wipes and return", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A wipe resets the active fight after ten seconds without living engaged members in the arena. Completed courts and cleared trash remain saved; a failed attempt does not reopen defeated courts.", "Keep the dragon in its court. A six-second leash warning gives the raid time to return before the attempt resets.", "The expedition lasts eight hours and has a separate 48-hour replay timer. Saved return, when enabled, keeps the original clocks."}}}},
  ["north-tov-broken-accord-nevederia"] = {overview = {"A seasonal North ToV side raid tuned for 24–36 level-60 characters, with up to three characters per player.", "Break six court oaths, then challenge Vulak's final judgment. Clear calls, fixed camps and assigned jobs give each three-character team time to respond."}, roles = {{id = "tank", label = "Tanks", tips = {"Move with the raid on each IN or OUT call. The dragon anchors during the warning; rebuild a controlled position after impact."}}, {id = "healer", label = "Healers and curers", tips = {"Move all healer characters before casting through the warning. Cold pulses resume between assignments, so top up before the next move."}}, {id = "damage", label = "Damage dealers", tips = {"IN means Dais Warden; OUT means Arch Warden. Move your whole team into the named camp and resume damage once every character is safe."}}, {id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Assign jobs by three-character team where possible. Read the named target, camp and countdown; check every character rather than moving only your main.", "Start each deadline healthy. A 75%-maximum-HP failure leaves little room for existing damage or the dragon's next attack."}}}, phases = {{label = "Break the oath", trigger = "Challenge to victory", description = "Resolve the court's repeating assignment on its 40-second cadence while maintaining damage and healing. There is no health-based phase change."}}, abilities = {{name = "Hoarfrost Reversal", summary = "Move to the announced fixed safe camp within ten seconds. IN and OUT alternate, starting with IN; follow the named landmark rather than estimating distance from the dragon.", description = {"Move to the announced fixed safe camp within ten seconds. IN and OUT alternate, starting with IN; follow the named landmark rather than estimating distance from the dragon.", "At impact, living players outside the announced camp's 20-unit radius take 75% of their maximum HP. Stand on the camp's floor with clear line of sight. The tank moves with the raid while the dragon anchors and stops summoning for the assignment."}, tags = {}, roles = {"everyone"}}, {name = "Cold pulse", summary = "Recurring raid damage between assignments.", description = {"A routine raid pulse is scheduled every 25 seconds. Assignment warnings, wards and recovery postpone it; missed pulses do not build into a burst."}, tags = {"raid damage"}, roles = {"healer", "everyone"}}}, sections = {{title = "Entry and raid preparation", paragraphs = {"This side raid requires active Season 1 characters of level 55 or higher, with both personal and server Velious access. Combat and equipment are designed around level 60."}, bullets = {"In the public Temple of Veeshan, the raid leader asks Echo of the First Brood for The Broken Accord with 12–36 eligible characters. Each member then says ready to enter to the Echo.", "Inside, the expedition leader says challenge to the selected Oath Witness. Fight the six courts in any order, one at a time; completing all six reveals Vulak. Challenge his Oath Witness when ready.", "The first challenge locks the raid's combat budget, with a 24-character minimum and a 36-character maximum. A 12-character request keeps the 24-character tuning floor and both six-character soak requirements. Later roster changes do not reduce that budget."}}, {title = "Positioning and warnings", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"IN: Dais Warden. OUT: Arch Warden. Each safe camp has a 20-unit radius; move every living character to the camp announced in chat.", "Use the named stationary landmarks on their flat floor, with clear line of sight. A matching camp icon confirms that a character counts as inside. Circles are an extra cue; follow chat calls and countdowns even when terrain makes them hard to see."}}, {title = "Timing and damage pressure", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The first assignment begins 40 seconds after the challenge. Subsequent assignments follow a 40-second cadence when the fight is ready.", "After an assignment resolves, there is an eight-second recovery before another scripted assignment or routine pulse. Boss melee generally continues. A failure dealing 75% to the current tank briefly pauses boss melee for two seconds.", "Percentage failures remove the stated share of maximum HP and bypass mitigation and absorption. They can kill an injured character; no one-HP survival floor applies. Recover before the next call.", "Soft enrage begins at eight minutes, adding 10% melee and another 10% every 30 seconds. Combined scripted melee increases cap at 50%."}}, {title = "Wipes and return", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A wipe resets the active fight after ten seconds without living engaged members in the arena. Completed courts and cleared trash remain saved; a failed attempt does not reopen defeated courts.", "Keep the dragon in its court. A six-second leash warning gives the raid time to return before the attempt resets.", "The expedition lasts eight hours and has a separate 48-hour replay timer. Saved return, when enabled, keeps the original clocks."}}}},
  ["templeveeshan-lord-feshlak"] = {overview = {"Engaging Lord Feshlak also brings the linked named guards into combat."}, roles = {{id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Prepare tanks or control for the linked guards before the pull."}}}, phases = {}, abilities = {}, sections = {{title = "Encounter plan", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"If still alive, Bryrym and Vukuz immediately add the puller to their hate lists.", "The quest script defines this linked pull but does not add a timed health-phase sequence."}}}},
  ["north-tov-broken-accord-feshlak"] = {overview = {"A seasonal North ToV side raid tuned for 24–36 level-60 characters, with up to three characters per player.", "Break six court oaths, then challenge Vulak's final judgment. Clear calls, fixed camps and assigned jobs give each three-character team time to respond."}, roles = {{id = "tank", label = "Tanks", tips = {"Hold Feshlak steady and call the named tank clearly. Changing tanks does not cure Venom Ledger on the original target."}}, {id = "healer", label = "Healers and curers", tips = {"Assign a primary poison curer and a backup. Remove all eight counters within 12 seconds; clerics, druids and shamans can use Counteract Poison."}}, {id = "damage", label = "Damage dealers", tips = {"Keep attacking while the cure team works. Poison pulses affect the raid between assignments; tell healers promptly if your team needs recovery."}}, {id = "everyone", label = "Everyone", tips = {"Assign jobs by three-character team where possible. Read the named target, camp and countdown; check every character rather than moving only your main.", "Start each deadline healthy. A 75%-maximum-HP failure leaves little room for existing damage or the dragon's next attack."}}}, phases = {{label = "Break the oath", trigger = "Challenge to victory", description = "Resolve the court's repeating assignment on its 45-second cadence while maintaining damage and healing. There is no health-based phase change."}}, abilities = {{name = "Venom Ledger", summary = "Cure all eight poison counters from the named tank within twelve seconds. Clerics, druids and shamans can perform the assignment using Counteract Poison.", description = {"Cure all eight poison counters from the named tank within twelve seconds. Clerics, druids and shamans can perform the assignment using Counteract Poison.", "If any counters remain at expiry, the tank takes 75% of maximum HP and the rest of the raid takes 25%; the debuff then clears. Death, disconnecting or zoning also fails the assignment at its original deadline."}, tags = {}, roles = {"everyone"}}, {name = "Poison pulse", summary = "Recurring raid damage between assignments.", description = {"A routine raid pulse is scheduled every 25 seconds. Assignment warnings, wards and recovery postpone it; missed pulses do not build into a burst."}, tags = {"raid damage"}, roles = {"healer", "everyone"}}}, sections = {{title = "Entry and raid preparation", paragraphs = {"This side raid requires active Season 1 characters of level 55 or higher, with both personal and server Velious access. Combat and equipment are designed around level 60."}, bullets = {"In the public Temple of Veeshan, the raid leader asks Echo of the First Brood for The Broken Accord with 12–36 eligible characters. Each member then says ready to enter to the Echo.", "Inside, the expedition leader says challenge to the selected Oath Witness. Fight the six courts in any order, one at a time; completing all six reveals Vulak. Challenge his Oath Witness when ready.", "The first challenge locks the raid's combat budget, with a 24-character minimum and a 36-character maximum. A 12-character request keeps the 24-character tuning floor and both six-character soak requirements. Later roster changes do not reduce that budget."}}, {title = "Positioning and warnings", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"Keep healers and the designated poison curers within range of the current tank. There is no movement camp for Venom Ledger.", "Use the named stationary landmarks on their flat floor, with clear line of sight. A matching camp icon confirms that a character counts as inside. Circles are an extra cue; follow chat calls and countdowns even when terrain makes them hard to see."}}, {title = "Timing and damage pressure", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"The first assignment begins 45 seconds after the challenge. Subsequent assignments follow a 45-second cadence when the fight is ready.", "After an assignment resolves, there is an eight-second recovery before another scripted assignment or routine pulse. Boss melee generally continues. A failure dealing 75% to the current tank briefly pauses boss melee for two seconds.", "Percentage failures remove the stated share of maximum HP and bypass mitigation and absorption. They can kill an injured character; no one-HP survival floor applies. Recover before the next call.", "Soft enrage begins at eight minutes, adding 10% melee and another 10% every 30 seconds. Combined scripted melee increases cap at 50%."}}, {title = "Wipes and return", paragraphs = {}, bullets = {"A wipe resets the active fight after ten seconds without living engaged members in the arena. Completed courts and cleared trash remain saved; a failed attempt does not reopen defeated courts.", "Keep the dragon in its court. A six-second leash warning gives the raid time to return before the attempt resets.", "The expedition lasts eight hours and has a separate 48-hour replay timer. Saved return, when enabled, keeps the original clocks."}}}},
}
